## TIẾNG ANH · 16:30–17:00 — Thứ Năm: Câu hỏi phỏng vấn

### 16:30–16:40 · Shadowing

### 16:40–16:55 · Trả lời có ghi âm

**Câu hỏi tuần này:** *"Tell me about a performance problem you solved."*

Đây là câu bạn **đã có sẵn hai câu chuyện** — một từ Firegroup, một từ tuần này. Dùng câu chuyện Firegroup làm chính vì nó ở môi trường production thật, rồi nhắc câu chuyện thứ hai làm bằng chứng thói quen.

> *"The one I'd pick is a bundle size problem at Firegroup. Our app was around forty-five megabytes and install conversion was suffering, especially on cheaper Android devices where storage is tight.*
> *First thing I did was measure rather than guess. I ran a bundle analysis and found three things: we were pulling in an entire icon library for about six icons, several PNG assets had never been compressed, and there were dependencies still bundled that nobody had imported in months.*
> *I fixed them one at a time and measured after each change, so I knew what actually helped. We ended up at twenty-eight megabytes — about a thirty-seven percent reduction.*
> *The interesting part was what didn't work. I'd assumed code splitting would be a big win, and it barely moved the number, because our screens were all small. That taught me to measure before committing to an approach.*
> *I've kept that habit. On my current project I've got a document with before-and-after numbers for every optimisation, including the ones that made no difference."*

**Cấu trúc:** vấn đề → đo trước → sửa từng cái → kết quả có số → **cái không hiệu quả** → thói quen còn giữ. Câu áp chót là câu làm nên khác biệt.

### 16:55–17:00 · 5 từ mới

| Từ / cụm | Nghĩa | Câu mẫu |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `move the needle` | tạo khác biệt thật sự | *What actually moved the needle was…* |
| `barely` (adv) | hầu như không | *It barely moved the number.* |
| `storage is tight` | bộ nhớ chật | *On devices where storage is tight.* |
| `one at a time` | từng cái một | *I fixed them one at a time.* |
| `commit to an approach` | dốc sức theo một hướng | *Measure before committing to an approach.* |

